Z||000000||CHOWITT31||01-31-2001||11:48 AM||||Hi folks I hope someone out there can answer this.<BR>Does anyone know what exactly what work was done concerning the recal for the 85 fiero's with the L4 engine, TSB88C23<BR>I am trying to determine if the work was done on my car.<BR>I called pontiac and the women I spoke with could not verify anything.<BR>Is the anything that I could look at visualy to determine if this was done?<BR>Thanks<BR>ken||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||01-31-2001||12:58 PM||||There is supposed to be a decal on the trunk lid though I've never seen one. One quick check is to see if there is a rubber strip between the trunk lid and the rear window glass, this was to be removed as part of the recall.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Steven||01-31-2001||01:54 PM||||And if there is no decal, that may not mean anything. One of the recalls done on my car, the tech. wrote the recall number on the underside of my deck lid in red paint pen. The other recall number was writen on masking tape and stuck on the underside of the deck lid so that when the lid was closed, it would be in the truck area not getting wet.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||01-31-2001||11:38 PM||||there is a summary of that recall in my cave. start with that.||||reg||1
Z||000004||CHOWITT31||02-01-2001||05:43 AM||||Thanks for all the info guys.<BR>judging from what you guys said to look for and all the great info in ogre's cave it looks like the work has been preformed.<BR>SEE YA<BR>KEN||||reg||1
